{
  "id": "c18",
  "title": "Stacks and Queues",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "c18-l1",
      "title": "Push and Pop",
      "xp": 15,
      "intro": [
        "A stack is like a pile of plates: you put things on top (push) and take them off the top (pop). The last one in is the first one out.",
        "With an array it takes three lines: int stack[100]; int top = 0;, push is stack[top++] = x;, and pop is stack[--top].",
        "Stacks are everywhere: the PDP-11 kept function calls on a stack, and \"undo\" in an editor is a stack of changes."
      ],
      "example": {
        "code": [
          "#include <stdio.h>",
          "",
          "char stack[100];",
          "int top = 0;",
          "",
          "void push(char c) {",
          "    stack[top++] = c;",
          "}",
          "",
          "char pop() {",
          "    return stack[--top];",
          "}",
          "",
          "int main() {",
          "    char *word = \"unix\";",
          "    int i;",
          "    for (i = 0; word[i] != '\\0'; i++)",
          "        push(word[i]);",
          "    while (top > 0)",
          "        putchar(pop());",
          "    putchar('\\n');",
          "    return 0;",
          "}"
        ],
        "output": [
          "xinu"
        ]
      },
      "exercises": [
        {
          "id": "c18-l1-e1",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "What comes out of a stack first?",
          "options": [
            "The last thing pushed",
            "The first thing pushed",
            "The smallest",
            "A random one"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "Last in, first out: LIFO."
        },
        {
          "id": "c18-l1-e2",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "prompt": "In the example, why is \"unix\" printed as \"xinu\"?",
          "options": [
            "The stack gives the letters back in reverse order",
            "putchar reverses",
            "The loop counts down",
            "It's a bug"
          ],
          "answer": 0,
          "explanation": "x went in last, so it comes out first."
        },
        {
          "id": "c18-l1-e3",
          "type": "fill_blank",
          "prompt": "Push x onto the stack.",
          "code": [
            "    stack[top___] = x;"
